WEBVTT

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:10.000
Many companies give their users more than
one app, and each app asks them to sign in.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.610
With browser login, users
sign in once on their device,

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.830
and their other apps can use that login.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.540
You choose how each app signs in, in
the browser config section of the app

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:29.480
configuration file.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.740
In the private mode, which is the default,
users sign in inside the app, and nothing is

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.500
remembered. In the persistent
mode, users also sign in inside

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.720
the app, and the app remembers
the login for next time.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.960
In the auth session mode, users sign
in through the device browser instead.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.660
This is the mode that lets one
login work across all of your apps.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:05.130
When the first app starts the login, the
device browser opens the sign-in page of

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.210
your identity provider.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:12.170
The user enters their password, and the
browser keeps the identity provider session.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:19.070
The user taps Continue to App, and the
browser takes them back to the first app,

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:25.320
signed in. Later, a second app
on the same device starts its

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.860
login in the same browser.

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:32.660
The identity provider already knows the
user, so the password page is skipped.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:38.600
The user taps continue to app,
and the second app is signed in

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.240
too, with its own app session.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.890
For this to work, both apps use the
auth session mode and the same identity

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:51.000
provider.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.810
To turn this on, set the auth mode to auth session
in the app configuration file.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:04.400
Then set the custom URL scheme in config.json
to your app ID, so the browser can

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.000
return to your app.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:14.950
You can also choose where links open,
in a browser window over your app, in a page inside
your app, or in the device browser.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:21.650
Links that open in the device browser can
use the same login, so users are not asked

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:26.910
to sign in again. After you change
these settings, build the app again.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:33.550
With Browser login, your users sign in
once and move between your apps without

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:34.310
signing you again.
